       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses that high risk severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses can cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **A typo or unit slip:** the usual doses are 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. Starting doses are 2.5\u20135 mg, and 2.5 mg is common for frail or older patients. I can enter whichever dose you choose.\n- **Intentional 50 mg:** tell me and add a note giving the rationale. I'll enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably still flag it.\n\nTell me the dose and I'll enter it right away."
